  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of policies and programme promoting sustainable livelihoods and incorporating gender responsive strategies for natural resources and ecosystems management.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2017">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">4</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	30,000 ha area in high Himalayan region brought under effective management 
2.	Atleast 03 innovative decentralized energy solutions demonstrated to reduce dependency on natural resources
3.	100 youth trained on sustainable natural resource management, monitoring and surveillance of biodiversity 
4.	Capacity building of 100 frontline staff conducted on wildlife enforcement mechanism and mitigation of wildlife crime &amp; illegal trade 
5.	800 households supported for implementing improved and diversified livelihood strategies in 6 landscapes across 3 states and 1 Union Territory 
6.	Human Wildlife Conflicts in the project landscape reduced by atleast 20% through demonstration of innovative solutions</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Approx. 30, 000 ha area in the Himalayan region brought under effective management through implementation of site-specific management actions.
2. Innovative decentralized Solar solutions demonstrated in Uttarakhand &amp; Sikkim (Solarized Primary Health Center). Energy efficient solutions introduced under smart school initiative in the high range Himalayan Landscapes.
3. 126 community members trained on sustainable natural resource management, monitoring and surveillance.
4. Capacity building of 100 front line staff has been conducted in combating wildlife Crime and Illegal trade
5. 1500 beneficiaries has been supported for implementing improved and diversified livelihood strategies and natural resource management. 
